  "term": "whole-channel",
  "definition": "Whole-channel information refers to information drawn across all channels or feature streams in a model, rather than from one channel alone. In the source, a multi-head self-attention mechanism is used to capture this across-channel information because it is described as important for improving prediction performance.",
